LAST_SUCCESS=Phase 1 complete (link+receive+send+persist, desktop + on-device link/receive). Phase 2 architecture DECIDED (user): WIT-decoupled signal-engine (exports wart:signal/chat) + signal-ui (imports chat + skiko-gfx, dioxus/Compose). Contract + plan written to tasks/67.
NOTES=Phase 2 = engine+UI as two composed components (WAC), UI toolkit-agnostic. Contract wart:signal/chat: init/poll-events->list<event>/send(text)/history/state; event = message|link-url|linked|connected|disconnected. GATING FINDING (verified from wstd src): wstd::block_on creates+clears reactor per call -> spawned tasks DON'T survive across component-export calls + no guest code runs between calls -> engine needs a PERSISTENT minimal step-executor (built in init, stepped non-blocking per poll-events via wasi:io/poll 0-timeout) and the wart-wasi-shims pollable-await (tls.rs::schedule -> wstd::runtime::AsyncPollable) must bind to THAT executor instead of wstd's. wstd stepping methods are private -> roll our own ~150-200 line executor. BUILD ORDER: (1) repros/signal-engine refactor signal-link -> component exporting chat over persistent executor (reuse store.rs/persist.rs/shims); (2) repros/signal-ui dioxus-canvas guest importing chat (history+poll-events render, input->send, QR from link-url); (3) WAC compose + on-device. dioxus-canvas at crates/dioxus-canvas (launch! macro, host-callback render model). Existing working signal client: repros/signal-link (CLI, in-memory+persist). Memory: project_signal_client_architecture, project_signal_wasip2_transport_swap. Build: PROTOC=~/tools/protoc/bin/protoc cargo build --target wasm32-wasip2 --release.
